;; Reviewed 2026-10-10 (written by Claude, from design sections 14 and
;; 16 and the guest runs; for the user's review). Why this is right:
;; - The lines before the last are the host's under -O2: SHORT and CHR
;;   of values that fit are the same on the VAX.
;; - The last statement, SHORT(1.0D300), cannot be done on the VAX:
;;   SHORT of a LONGREAL is CVTGF, unchecked (design section 14, item
;;   9), and 1.0D300 is past the largest F_floating number (about
;;   1.7E38), so CVTGF is a floating overflow fault, not LLVM's
;;   infinity. The program stops there, without its last line (.err and
;;   .status say how).
;; - For every build, with and without -range-checks; expected-vax-
;;   rangechecks-OC-1.out and expected-vax-rangechecks-OC-range-
;;   checks-1.out override it under -OC, whose first two lines differ:
;;   INTEGER is 32 bits there.
32767
-32768
127
-128
2147483647
-2147483648
0
255
127
